  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 228 AM Sunday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Showers will shift east of I-95 this morning. \nPartly sunny this afternoon, only an isolated shower (10 percent). \n\nThe base of the mid/upper level trough will pass overhead this \nmorning. Subsidence in the rear of this feature will lower the \nshower chances to very isolated this afternoon (less than 10 percent \nat any one point). The exception may be along and east of I-95 where \nthe showers may linger through late morning today. The main cold \nfront will shift through the area this evening and overnight. This \nwill be followed by cooler and drier advection from the northeast \nbeginning Monday. Highs today will generally be in the mid to upper \n80s. Lows tonight in the mid 60s to around70. Highs Monday will be \nin the lower to mid 80s.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... Cooler and less humid with a NE flow this \nupcoming week. \n\nStrong upper ridging is expected to set up over the Tennessee Valley \nearly this week, then shift back westward toward the Southern Plains \nby Thursday and Friday. This will keep it dry this week over NC.\n\nA 1030 mb surface high pressure will build down into the mid-\nAtlantic states from the Great Lakes Monday, then slowly shift east \noff the New England coast by mid-week. The SW extension of the high \nwill extend over NC keeping conditions dry and mild. Lows in the mid \n50s to lower 60s Monday through Thursday, with highs in the lower to \nmid 80s.",
